commit c8b2ff0bc69d80a0bdcc5f957e9b8d023d743864
Author: Yixun-Hu <yixunhu21@gmail.com>
Date:   Sun Sep 27 05:35:56 2026 -0400

    exp11 fix3 (GREEN): recovery is owned, serialised, idempotent and explicit
    
    abort_recovery narrows the abort path to what this invocation may act on: an attempt
    that is already published as final or already carries a completion is PRESERVED with
    its directory, completion and link untouched, and the finalizer's own cause stands -
    a malformed recovery does not establish that a finished run failed. Full mode keeps
    aborting unconditionally, since it launched the attempt it aborts.
    
    take_lock serialises alias resolution, validation, finalization and promotion per arm
    with an atomic mkdir lock that full-mode promotion also takes; a held lock refuses
    immediately with the owner and liveness in the message, a trap releases it on every
    exit path, and a stale lock is cleared only by an explicit --break-lock, never on a
    timer. already_published makes a same-target recovery a no-op ("ALREADY PUBLISHED"),
    and check_final_conflict refuses a DIFFERENT existing final unless --replace-final is
    given, logging the replaced target before the atomic mv. Alias resolution and the
    attempt_*/arm-root checks are unchanged. The two full-mode goldens are regenerated for
    the new LOCK line.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

