commit 16b1eff9921e55aef40aaf352740208931c4b7fe
Author: Yixun-Hu <yixunhu21@gmail.com>
Date:   Sun Sep 27 06:52:49 2026 -0400

    exp11 fix4 (GREEN): terminating signal handlers and lock generations
    
    on_signal does ownership-safe cleanup, logs SIGNAL <name> and exits 128+n, so a handler
    ends the invocation instead of returning into finalization or promotion; the EXIT trap
    keeps the cleanup, and not_interrupted guards both protected steps in both modes so
    nothing downstream can run after a handler fired.
    
    The lock now carries a GENERATION: take_lock writes pid + a per-invocation nonce into
    the owner file, and release_lock removes the directory only while that nonce is still
    there - never on the process-local flag alone - so an earlier owner's exit can no longer
    delete its successor's lock. break_lock takes the generation the caller OBSERVED,
    refuses a live owner pid, refuses if the lock has changed generation since, and
    serialises replacement by atomically renaming that specific lock aside (the target is
    named for the observed generation, so a second breaker with the same observation
    collides and a late one finds the source gone); if what moved was not what was observed
    it is put back and the breaker refuses. A bounded, path-only barrier hook lets the tests
    interleave two breakers deterministically without evaluating anything.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

